        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.337,
            0.775,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": "What will the fraction be when $\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 0 }$ is split into 10 equal parts? It will be $\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 0 0 }$ , i.e., a thousand such parts make up a unit."
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.415,
            0.831,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_chart_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.801,
            0.848,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "Just as when we extend to the left of 10,000, we get bigger place values at each step, we can also extend to the right of $\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 0 0 }$ , getting smaller place values at each step."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
